   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_AUT_SALZ_01">Hotel Mirabell</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Salzburg</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Austria</addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1928-08-06">6.8.928</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <p>Dear Budgen: Your letter has been following me around the Tyrol. We are sorry to have been out of <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris</name> when you passed through but hope <name type="person" key="budg96">Mrs Budgen</name> and yourself will be over again. I am <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">glad you like Shaun</seg>. By the way, I hope <hi rend="underline">transition</hi> <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">settled up</seg>? I asked them to do so.</p>        <salute>sincerely yours</salute>        <signed>
                        <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                    </signed> </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Probably a reference to “Continuation of a Work in Progress” from <name type="work">transition</name> no. 13 (Summer 1928), 5–32, which contained an early version of <name type="work" key="W_FINNEGANSWAKE">FW</name> III.2.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Budgen’s article, “The Work in Progress of James Joyce and Old Norse Poetry”, was published in <name type="work">transition</name> no. 13 (Summer 1928), 209–13. In a <rs type="letter" key="L_69648">letter to Budgen of 27 May 1928</rs>, JJ noted that “I asked them to send you a cheque” (<name type="work">LIII</name> 177).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
